1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,507
Zinc, which gives up electrons easily, has a positive oxidation potential.

2
00:00:05,507 --> 00:00:08,085
Copper prefers to take electrons back.

3
00:00:08,085 --> 00:00:13,906
To avoid confusion, the world agreed to tabulate only reduction potentials.

4
00:00:13,906 --> 00:00:18,294
An oxidation potential is just the same number with the sign flipped.

